  "limitations": [
    "No browser array layout or native mismatch was directly captured. Standalone describe() observations validate synthetic equivalent constructions, not each browser allocation.",
    "The tagged variant adds an object allocation and length truncation; the int32 variant adds coercion instructions. Timing/code shape and array storage all change, so passing controls do not prove the exact defective instruction.",
    "Bitwise coercion is valid only for this synthetic 1/2048 data set. It corrupts fractions, negative zero and large unsigned values and is not an editor fix.",
    "All runs disable JIT and use a 10000-iteration budget with zero retries; these are diagnostic experiments, not production qualification.",
    "The array-zero symptom remains distinct from the original editor false upper-bound comparison until execution evidence links them."
